  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nAbove normal upper ridging continues to promote well above normal\nsurface heat, and in spite of the lower dewpoints and greater \nmixing, we're still seeing limited to elevated heat danger in the \nnear term ahead of an approaching cold front. However, relief from\nthe heat is on the way. The cold front is expected to move \nthrough the area by Tuesday night/Wednesday, and this will bring \ntemperatures and humidity levels that are much more typical of \nSeptember. \n\nAside from the heat, we will be monitoring for the potential of a\nfew strong/severe storms ahead of the cold front early this week.\nFor Monday, per SPC, there is a marginal severe risk for a few \npulse severe storms during peak heating over northern portions of \nthe area. For Tuesday, there is currently no official SPC severe \noutlook in our forecast area, but it wouldn't be a surprise to see\neastern portions of the area enter the picture for a possible \nmarginal risk as we get closer in time. Looking ahead for the late\nweek into next weekend, as mentioned, drier conditions can be \nexpected with \"less hot\" temperatures. Overall, weather impacts \nshould mostly be tied to early week heat and convective potential.\n/EC/",
